<emu-clause id="formal-agents">
  <h1>Waiter Lists and Critical Sections</h1>
  <p>The agent cluster's store of WaiterList Records and their critical sections (<emu-xref href="#sec-waiterlist-records"></emu-xref>), and the switches between its agents.</p>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-waiterlistfor" name="WaiterListFor">
    <emu-signature>WaiterListFor(_block_: a Shared Data Block, _i_: a non-negative integer): a WaiterList Record</emu-signature>
    <p>The WaiterList Record that the agent cluster's store of WaiterList Records holds for (_block_, _i_) (<emu-xref href="#sec-waiterlist-records"></emu-xref>): the same Record for the same _block_ and _i_. Until its critical section is first entered, its [[Waiters]] is an empty List and its [[MostRecentLeaveEvent]] is ~empty~.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-acquirecriticalsection" name="AcquireCriticalSection">
    <emu-signature>AcquireCriticalSection(_waiterList_: a WaiterList Record): ~unused~</emu-signature>
    <p>Waits until no agent is in the critical section for _waiterList_, then enters it, without allowing any other agent to enter (<emu-xref href="#sec-waiterlist-records"></emu-xref>). With the surrounding agent the only agent, the wait ends at once unless the surrounding agent is in that critical section, when it never ends.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-releasecriticalsection" name="ReleaseCriticalSection">
    <emu-signature>ReleaseCriticalSection(_waiterList_: a WaiterList Record): ~unused~</emu-signature>
    <p>The surrounding agent leaves the critical section for _waiterList_, which it is in (<emu-xref href="#sec-waiterlist-records"></emu-xref>).</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-enteredcriticalsections" name="EnteredCriticalSections">
    <emu-signature>EnteredCriticalSections(): a List of WaiterList Records</emu-signature>
    <p>A new List of the WaiterList Records whose critical section the surrounding agent is in (<emu-xref href="#sec-waiterlist-records"></emu-xref>), in an order that uses must not depend on.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-suspendagentuntil" name="SuspendAgentUntil">
    <emu-signature>SuspendAgentUntil(_waiterList_: a WaiterList Record, _timeoutTime_: an extended mathematical value): ~unused~</emu-signature>
    <p>Suspends the surrounding agent until the time is _timeoutTime_, or until another agent performs NotifyWaiter(_waiterList_, _w_) for a Waiter Record _w_ whose [[AgentSignifier]] is the surrounding agent's signifier (via a call to `Atomics.notify`), whichever comes first (<emu-xref href="#sec-suspendthisagent"></emu-xref> step 7). The suspension takes effect together with the LeaveCriticalSection(_waiterList_) performed just before it, in such a way that a notification that arrives after the critical section is exited but before the suspension takes effect is not lost. With the surrounding agent the only agent, it wakes only by the timeout, so never where _timeoutTime_ is +∞.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-suspendthisagent" steps="7" hashes="90550a66f69f884aab50dbfd6d4f202ce364e1021524afbd633dd962827ad1b5">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Perform LeaveCriticalSection(_waiterList_).
      1. Perform SuspendAgentUntil(_waiterList_, _waiterRecord_.[[TimeoutTime]]).
      1. Repeat, while AgentWoken() is *false*,
        1. Perform AgentInterleave().
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-reading>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-notifywaiter" steps="2.a" hashes="b8df3f1bbdf60b23de35d730fc2c46464b93dfae40793a3c13cc7f3f85b21c3d">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Perform WakeAgent(_waiterRecord_.[[AgentSignifier]]).
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-reading>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-wakeagent" name="WakeAgent">
    <emu-signature>WakeAgent(_sig_: an agent signifier): ~unused~</emu-signature>
    <p>Wakes the agent whose signifier is _sig_ from suspension (<emu-xref href="#sec-notifywaiter"></emu-xref> step 2.a): its latest SuspendAgentUntil, if performed before this, ends, so that AgentWoken() is *true* for it and it resumes execution in SuspendThisAgent. It has no other effect.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-switchtoagent" name="SwitchToAgent">
    <emu-signature>SwitchToAgent(_agent_: an Agent Record): ~unused~</emu-signature>
    <p>Saves the execution context stack in the surrounding agent's Agent Record's [[ParkedStack]], makes _agent_.[[ParkedStack]] the execution context stack and _agent_ the surrounding agent. The execution context that was running before is the one whose evaluation a following Resume suspends. _agent_ is not the surrounding agent, and the surrounding agent is in no critical section.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-hostselectagent" name="HostSelectAgent">
    <emu-signature>HostSelectAgent(_agent_: an Agent Record, _n_: a non-negative integer): an Agent Record or ~empty~</emu-signature>
    <p>The host's choice of the agent of _agent_'s agent cluster that runs next, after _agent_ has added _n_ events to its [[EventList]]: an agent other than _agent_ that is not suspended or has been woken, or ~empty~ if the host lets _agent_ continue (<emu-xref href="#sec-forward-progress"></emu-xref>).</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-agenttimeout" name="AgentTimeout">
    <emu-signature>AgentTimeout(): a non-negative integer</emu-signature>
    <p>The time the host advances the agent cluster's clock to while no other agent can run and the surrounding agent is suspended: the earliest time at which a suspended agent wakes, never before the present time.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-agentwoken" name="AgentWoken">
    <emu-signature>AgentWoken(): a Boolean</emu-signature>
    <p>Whether the surrounding agent, suspended by its latest SuspendAgentUntil(_waiterList_, _timeoutTime_), has been woken: by a WakeAgent of its signifier performed after it, or by the time reaching _timeoutTime_.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-agentnextjob" name="AgentNextJob">
    <emu-signature>AgentNextJob(): a non-negative integer or ~empty~</emu-signature>
    <p>The host's next job for the surrounding agent (<emu-xref href="#sec-jobs"></emu-xref>): the scheduling of a Job of this agent, ready to be performed now, that has not been taken, else ~empty~. The scheduling is identified by an integer the host gives; taking it is taking that Job.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-agentpreparejob" name="AgentPrepareJob">
    <emu-signature>AgentPrepareJob(_k_: a non-negative integer): a Job Abstract Closure</emu-signature>
    <p>Performs the host-defined preparation steps of the Job the scheduling _k_ scheduled, with the execution context stack empty, and returns that Job.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-agentcleanupjob" name="AgentCleanupJob">
    <emu-signature>AgentCleanupJob(_k_: a non-negative integer): ~unused~</emu-signature>
    <p>Performs the host-defined cleanup steps of the Job the scheduling _k_ scheduled; the execution context stack is then empty.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-clause id="formal-agent-interleave" type="abstract operation">
    <h1>AgentInterleave ( ): ~unused~</h1>
    <dl class="header">
      <dt>description</dt>
      <dd>A point at which the host may run another agent of the surrounding agent's cluster (<emu-xref href="#sec-forward-progress"></emu-xref>): the surrounding agent's execution context stack is set aside until an agent switches back to it. Agents switch only here, never inside a critical section.</dd>
    </dl>
    <emu-alg>
      1. Assert: EnteredCriticalSections() is empty.
      1. Let _agent_ be the Agent Record of the surrounding agent.
      1. Let _execution_ be _agent_.[[CandidateExecution]].
      1. Let _eventsRecord_ be the Agent Events Record of _execution_.[[EventsRecords]] whose [[AgentSignifier]] is AgentSignifier().
      1. Let _target_ be HostSelectAgent(_agent_, the number of elements in _eventsRecord_.[[EventList]]).
      1. If _target_ is ~empty~, then
        1. Perform AgentTimeout().
        1. Return ~unused~.
      1. Perform SwitchToAgent(_target_).
      1. Resume the running execution context, passing NormalCompletion(~unused~).
      1. Return ~unused~.
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-phrase id="ph-assert-critical" kind="step" rule="assert-critical">
    <emu-pattern>Assert: The surrounding agent is in the critical section for _waiterList_.</emu-pattern>
    <emu-params>_waiterList_: a WaiterList Record</emu-params>
    <emu-alg>
      1. Assert: EnteredCriticalSections() contains _waiterList_.
      1. Return ~unused~.
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-phrase>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-entercriticalsection" steps="1" hashes="b1e76d2c45462bf47734b54e9b606781f812aa8f4cda637b4854901c6e9196a4">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Assert: EnteredCriticalSections() is empty.
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-reading>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-getwaiterlist" steps="2" hashes="933e9824a641472046a10e1815bd30529db6f134dd6f9f3d1cf770c3afb51cec">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Return WaiterListFor(_block_, _i_).
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-reading>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-entercriticalsection" steps="2" hashes="d620e62a2fd16dec42ca868060095f0f039f4b7711c967066a7fd8dda0c809bd">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Perform AcquireCriticalSection(_waiterList_).
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-reading>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-entercriticalsection" steps="3.g" hashes="319c877de53c5594bb6bac423178789399adb35e7d23ad059335b412926523c1">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Append « _waiterList_.[[MostRecentLeaveEvent]], _enterEvent_ » to _eventsRecord_.[[AgentSynchronizesWith]].
    </emu-alg>
    <emu-note>
      <p>An ordered pair (_a_, _b_) is held as the List « _a_, _b_ ».</p>
    </emu-note>
  </emu-reading>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-leavecriticalsection" steps="8" hashes="4ee6afb1e367e806f2bf8f4b17e7cf3f60d77719b920853948b82909eab5e256">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Perform ReleaseCriticalSection(_waiterList_).
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-reading>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-createbytedatablock" steps="3" hashes="e5c8955beb844d73857da794aecd34fa768f3809c9f0a6653063b54301101df0">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Perform SetAllBytes(_dataBlock_, 0).
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-reading>

  <emu-phrase id="ph-type-pairs-of" kind="type" subject="_v_" rule="ht-pairs-of">
    <emu-pattern>pairs of _t_</emu-pattern>
    <p>An element of "a List of pairs of _t_": an ordered pair, held as a List of its two elements, each a _t_.</p>
    <emu-params>_t_: a type, _v_: anything</emu-params>
    <emu-alg>
      1. If _v_ is not a List, return *false*.
      1. If the number of elements in _v_ is not 2, return *false*.
      1. For each element _e_ of _v_, do
        1. If _e_ is not a _t_, return *false*.
      1. Return *true*.
    </emu-alg>
  </emu-phrase>
</emu-clause>
